------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled neuroimaging tools and model weights
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

medmcp-neuro-core wraps established third-party neuroimaging tools and
redistributes some of their pretrained weights/checkpoints (baked into the
published container image). Each remains under its own license and carries its
own citation requirements; if you use the results in research, please cite the
underlying methods (see the "Citation" section of README.md).

  - HD-BET (skull_strip) — brain extraction.
    Apache-2.0. https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/HD-BET
    Cite: Isensee et al., "Automated brain extraction of multi-sequence MRI
    using artificial neural networks", Human Brain Mapping (2019).
    doi:10.1002/hbm.24750

  - ANTs / ANTsPy (register_to_template, coregister, apply_transform) —
    image registration.
    Apache-2.0. https://github.com/ANTsX/ANTsPy
    Cite: Tustison et al., "The ANTsX ecosystem for quantitative biological and
    medical imaging", Scientific Reports 11:9068 (2021).
    doi:10.1038/s41598-021-87564-6

  - FastSurfer (segment_brain) — deep-learning whole-brain segmentation
    (FastSurferVINN, seg-only; no FreeSurfer license required).
    Apache-2.0. https://github.com/Deep-MI/FastSurfer
    Cite: Henschel et al., "FastSurfer - A fast and accurate deep learning based
    neuroimaging pipeline", NeuroImage 219:117012 (2020).
    doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2020.117012
    Henschel et al., "FastSurferVINN: Building resolution-independence into deep
    learning segmentation methods", NeuroImage 251:118933 (2022).
    doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2022.118933

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Standard-space templates
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - MNI152NLin2009cAsym (register_to_template default template), retrieved on
    first use from TemplateFlow and baked into the published container image.
    Distributed under the template's own license (see the LICENSE file in
    https://github.com/templateflow/tpl-MNI152NLin2009cAsym).
    Cite: Fonov et al., "Unbiased average age-appropriate atlases for pediatric
    studies", NeuroImage 54(1):313-327 (2011).
    doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2010.07.033
    Retrieved via TemplateFlow: Ciric et al., "TemplateFlow: FAIR-sharing of
    multi-scale, multi-species brain models", Nature Methods 19:1568-1571 (2022).
    doi:10.1038/s41592-022-01681-2

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Brain atlases (lesion_load_by_atlas)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Baked into the published container image under
/root/.medmcp_neuro_core/atlases/<name>/, each with an ATTRIBUTION.txt (source
URL, SHA-256, licence, changes) and the upstream licence file where one is
shipped. Only atlases whose licence permits redistribution are included; the
JHU (ICBM-DTI-81, white-matter tractography), FSL XTRACT, Juelich, Brainnetome
and Julich-Brain atlases are deliberately NOT bundled.

  - Pandora white matter atlas, TractSeg bundle set (pandora_tractseg).
    CC BY 4.0. https://github.com/MASILab/Pandora-WhiteMatterAtlas
    (commit 2caf44296666c13aa5c4d7d1c88d14fe553d9553), also on NITRC
    (https://www.nitrc.org/projects/pandora_atlas).
    Changes: the 4-D TractSeg.nii.gz is split into one 3-D file per bundle;
    values are unchanged.
    Cite: Hansen et al., "Pandora: 4-D white matter bundle population-based
    atlases derived from diffusion MRI fiber tractography", Neuroinformatics
    19:447-460 (2021). doi:10.1007/s12021-020-09497-1
    Built from Human Connectome Project (WU-Minn Consortium, 1U54MH091657),
    BLSA and Vanderbilt data.

  - HCP1065 population-probability tract atlas (hcp1065).
    CC BY-SA 4.0 (share-alike applies to these atlas files only, which are
    redistributed unmodified). https://github.com/frankyeh/data-atlas
    (release "hcp1065", hcp1065_prob_coverage_nifti.zip).
    Cite: Yeh FC, "Population-based tract-to-region connectome of the human
    brain and its hierarchical topology", Nat Commun 13:4933 (2022).
    doi:10.1038/s41467-022-32595-4
    Data were provided in part by the Human Connectome Project, WU-Minn
    Consortium (Principal Investigators: David Van Essen and Kamil Ugurbil;
    1U54MH091657) funded by the 16 NIH Institutes and Centers that support the
    NIH Blueprint for Neuroscience Research; and by the McDonnell Center for
    Systems Neuroscience at Washington University.

  - Schaefer 2018 cortical parcellations, 100/200/400 parcels, 7 networks
    (schaefer2018_100, schaefer2018_200, schaefer2018_400), MNI152NLin2009cAsym
    versions from TemplateFlow.
    MIT. Copyright (c) 2016 Computational Brain Imaging Group (CBIG).
    https://github.com/ThomasYeoLab/CBIG
    Cite: Schaefer et al., "Local-Global Parcellation of the Human Cerebral
    Cortex from Intrinsic Functional Connectivity MRI", Cerebral Cortex
    28(9):3095-3114 (2018). doi:10.1093/cercor/bhx179

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled libraries
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Python libraries redistributed inside the container image — including
PyTorch, nnU-Net (the engine HD-BET builds on), nibabel, nilearn (BSD-3, the
lesion_frequency_map figure), and their transitive
dependency closure — each remain under their own license; the full license texts
travel with each package's distribution.
